// index.malloy: this package's published surface.
//
// Publisher reads a package's index.malloy as the list of what it publishes,
// so publisher.json needs no "explores" key: the surface is whatever this
// file exports.
//
// `export { ... }` is the curation, and it is a real boundary rather than
// just a listing filter. A source named here is discoverable AND queryable.
// A source left out still compiles, and other models can import, join and
// extend it, but a direct query against it is refused with a 404 that says
// it is not on this surface. (Once a model carries an authorize or
// access_filter gate, that 404 reads the same as for a source that does not
// exist, so it cannot be used to find hidden names.) Add a name here to
// publish it; leave one out to keep it as an internal building block.
//
// To curate listings WITHOUT refusing queries, add "queryableSources": "all"
// to publisher.json: this file still decides what is listed, and every source
// stays queryable by name. Its one use is an authorize-gated source kept out
// of listings that authorized callers still query. See
// docs/discovery-and-access.md.

import "{{modelFile}}"

export { {{sourceName}} }
